# Wallpapers

### Computer / phone wallpapers (this thread)
Those are digital images, not wall coverings. Typical MDS/Dewey homes:

- **006.6** — Computer graphics
- **004** / **005** — General computing / software (collections of desktop backgrounds sometimes land here)
- **741.6** — Graphic design / commercial art
- **779** — Photographs (if the “wallpaper” is a nature or landscape photo)

### Physical wallpaper (wall covering)
Most common placements:

- **645.2** — Wall coverings (household furnishings: paper, fabric, vinyl on walls)
- **747.3** — Walls and window treatment (interior decoration: design, hanging, styles)

Related numbers will also see:

- **745** — Ornamental / decorative design (historic Dewey wording explicitly included wall paper with carpets and fabrics)
- **698.6** — Paperhanging as a building trade
- **676** — Pulp and paper technology (manufacture of the paper itself)

**Rule of thumb:** how-to / home-furnishing books → **645.2**. Design and interior-style books → **747** / **747.3**.
